    "unavailableNote": "Rows whose url starts with one of unavailableHosts were published on a host that no longer answers (the Swarm-Official organisation is suspended). The pages render them as being re-published instead of a dead button, and tools/check_downloads.mjs lists them as paused. Repoint url and checksums to louisinthesubway/swarm-releases as each file is uploaded again; the SHA-256 stays the same.",
    "pauseReasons": {
      "superseded-2026-10-02": "no longer connects to the network; install the current version."
    },
    "pauseNote": "An entry with \"paused\": \"<key of pauseReasons>\" (or a plain reason) is published but must not be offered: the pages draw \"A new version is being published\" instead of its buttons and checksum, and tools/check_downloads.mjs lists it as paused. A platform that also has an available entry without the flag shows that entry and hides the paused one, so adding the new rows is enough; delete the old rows (or the flag) when they go.",
    "note": "Download metadata for the Ecosystem block on the home page, the /ecosystem hub and the app pages. Mainnet builds are the downloads; testnet builds are kept under \"channel\": \"testnet\" and rendered in their own labelled section. After updating entries, run python tools/build_ecosystem.py and verify with --check. Every available entry must have a working URL, version, SHA-256 and byte size.",
    "windowsNotice": "Unsigned build — Windows SmartScreen will warn. Check the SHA-256.",
    "mobileNotice": "Mobile apps are wallets only — phones do not mine.",
    "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/Swarmcoin",
    "sourceNote": "Owner rule 2026-09-28: downloads are served from SWARM's own server (lwd-main.swarm.green/downloads/<tag>/<file>); github.com is never linked for a download. sourceUrl is the code; releasesUrl is only a record.",
